WEBVTT

00:01:26.375 --> 00:01:30.559
I'm going to teach you
how to stop a coup, OK?

00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:32.601
Now, where to begin?

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.768
Alright, how about this:

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:38.518
It turns out that one of the main
safeguards of US democracy

00:01:38.542 --> 00:01:40.851
is not in the constitution at all.

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:42.934
It's not in the law at all.

00:01:42.958 --> 00:01:46.184
It's actually just a little tradition,
it's a little custom.

00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:50.684
And yet, this one voluntary gesture

00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:52.226
is one of the main reasons

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.559
that you almost never have riots
and bloodshed and strife

00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:57.601
after a US election.

00:01:57.625 --> 00:02:00.309
What I'm talking about
is a concession speech.